## Cold setup evidence (fresh clone, isolated empty caches)

- Environment: fresh `git clone` of this branch; BUN_INSTALL_CACHE_DIR,
  UV_CACHE_DIR, UV_PYTHON_INSTALL_DIR all pointed at new empty directories.
- bun install --frozen-lockfile -> 86 packages fetched from the registry in
  5.1s, exit 0 (network preparation; ~300 MB cache populated).
- Host uv 0.9.5 with empty interpreter store: after excluding PATH
  interpreters, it STILL resolved and downloaded the pinned CPython 3.13.15
  on this host/date (live index lookup). This contradicts the recorded
  assumption in config/test-toolchain.json ("0.9.5's index predates it");
  the recorded >= 0.12.13 minimum stands and 0.9.5 behavior must not be
  relied on.
- Disposable uv==0.12.13 (pinned PyPI wheel, per the freeze's Linux proof):
  resolved and downloaded CPython 3.13.15 into the empty store, created the
  frozen native environment (13 locked packages), exit 0.
- Offline processing: with HTTP(S)_PROXY pointed at a dead address
  (127.0.0.1:9), `bun run verify` (169 tests OK), `bun run build` (exit 0),
  `bun run test:native` (196 passed), and the docs checks all passed —
  processing after install requires no network.

Cold setup evidence complete: network preparation (bun install; uv
interpreter/wheel provisioning) recorded separately from offline processing
(verify/build/native/docs checks behind a dead proxy). Remaining unproven:
a host where the tools themselves (bun, uv, compilers, browsers) have never
been installed — that install step is outside this repository's control.

